WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.534
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.968
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.400
[ Cheering and applause ]
You're here.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.334
You made it.
[ Whistling ]

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:07.868
Thank you for watching.

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.701
Well, guys, a new poll found

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:12.834
that President Biden's approval
rating has not been affected

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:14.701
by the classified
documents scandal.

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:18.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:19.634
Today, Biden said.
"In that case,

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:21.701
there's another 100 documents
stashed in the poolhouse.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:24.100
[ Laughter ]
Let's just get that out."

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.767
Right now, the White House is
like, "Alright, we just have

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:27.767
to keep Biden from singing
'Happy Birthday'

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.434
and it'll be smooth sailing
from here."

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:30.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:31.801
-♪ Happy birthday ♪

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:33.901
[ Laughter ]
♪ Dear Vavitz ♪

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:35.868
[ Cheering and applause ]
♪ Happy birthday ♪

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.901
♪ To you ♪

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:39.033
-Who?

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:39.734
Dear Mavah?

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:44.434
Meanwhile, the White House
is accusing Republicans

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:45.734
of political theater

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.234
because they've been
attacking Biden

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:49.200
for the handling
of classified documents,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.934
but gave former President Trump
a free pass.

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:53.701
Yeah, political theater.

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:55.901
Honestly, all this fighting
makes me want to run...

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.767
...and scream...

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.267
[ Laughter ]
The White House
says Republicans

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:03.267
will call Biden an...

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:05.701
...but then turn around,
say Trump is Wicked awesome

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.467
[ Laughter and applause ]
for doing the same thing.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.067
Or that Trump is...

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:10.801
...while Biden should be...

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.701
[ Laughter and applause ]
I mean, the story's everywhere.

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.033
Every morning I wake up,

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.868
Aida ["I eat a"] bowl of cereal.

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:19.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:22.000
When I turn on the
Newsies ["news he's"]

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.567
got another Six documents.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:24.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:26.701
Meanwhile, over in Congress,
George Santos is

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:27.767
The Lion King
["the lyin' king"]

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:28.968
[ Laughter ]
and the government

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.400
can barely afford...

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.467
[ Laughter ]
I mean, voting for speaker
of the House

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.200
left them Frozen
for a full week.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.334
[ Laughter ]
It's like...

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:39.467
...Parton gets more done
than you...

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:40.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:41.701
You got to start
working together.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.100
I don't care if you use
Jedi mind tricks

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.634
like Mark Hamill. Tons
of people are counting on you.

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:47.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.367
People from...

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.200
...Jersey Boys-ee ["Boise"]...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:56.400
...and over on the
West Side. Storytime's
over, though.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.934
[ Laughter ]
It's time to face...

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:01.601
[ Laughter ]
...because all this fighting
isn't...

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:02.968
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.033
[ Mouths "Thank you" ]

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.767
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:07.801
[ Whistling ]

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:11.934
-Preach!

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.367
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.934
Some more news
from Washington --

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.100
I heard that
Congressman George Santos

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.934
was just awarded seats
on two House committees,

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.634
including the Science, Space,
and Technology Committee.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:23.901
[ Booing and laughter ]
-[ Snickers ]

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:25.567
-A lot of people are saying
that he's not qualified.

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:28.901
I mean, just look at how he
defined some simple space terms.

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:32.033
For instance, when asked
to define cosmos, Santos said...

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:36.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:39.467
Next up, when asked to define
constellation, Santos said...

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.000
[ Laughter ]
-What?! What?!

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:47.467
Up next, when asked to define
orbit, Santos said...

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:51.267
[ Laughter and oohs ]

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.701
When asked to define celestial,
Santos said...

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.834
[ Laughter ]
-Really?

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:59.133
-Mama Celestial.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:01.701
And, finally, when asked
to define prism, Santos said...

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.167
-Oh.
-[ Indistinct ]

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:06.167
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.968
[ Indistinct ]
It got serious.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.334
Switching gears --
a new study found

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:15.634
that the COVID vaccine could
make Botox less effective.

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:19.100
[ Oohs and laughter ]

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.934
People who --

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.334
People who get Botox are upset
and the worst part is

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:24.834
you can actually see
that they're upset.

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.167
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:28.567
Their eyebrows are moving.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:29.834
Some sports news --

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:32.734
the LIV Golf tour is close
to securing a TV deal

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:34.434
with the CW network.

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:36.000
-[ Snicker ]
-And, if that happens,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.767
I think it's going to change
the way we look at golf.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.200
I mean, they already released
a teaser for the upcoming year.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.334
Watch this.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.267
♪ I don't want to wait ♪

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:46.300
♪ For our lives to be over ♪

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.367
♪ I want to know right now ♪

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.901
♪ What will it be ♪

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:52.601
♪ Sorry ♪

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:55.133
-♪ Do do do do ♪

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.501
♪ Do do do do ♪

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:57.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:57.801 --> 00:03:59.634
[ Cheering ]
-A little different.
-Wow.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.968
Well, over the past year,
due to supply chain issues,

00:04:05.968 --> 00:04:09.334
the prices of margarine
and butter have skyrocketed.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:11.334
So, if anyone's thinking
about getting their head stuck

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:12.767
in a banister, think twice.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:16.534
Right now, movie theaters
are like -- [ Inhales sharply ]

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:19.067
[ New York accent ]
Call us when the price
of motor oil goes up.

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:20.234
[ As Jerry Lewis ]
Oh, boy!

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:23.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.901
-[ Squelching ]

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:28.000
You want --
You want [ Mumbling ]?
[ Inhales sharply ]

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.467
Listen to this, everyone --

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:33.400
tax season is almost here
and, apparently,

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.801
the country is facing
a shortage of accountants.

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:37.234
[ Ohhs and oohs ]
-What?

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:39.000
-Let me get this straight --
we're currently short

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.868
on eggs, butter,
and accountants.

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:43.300
[ Laughter ]
And to that, I say,

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.267
what the hell are people
making their cakes out of?

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:48.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.067
[ Applause ]

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:52.033
Yeah, in the past two years,

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:54.834
more than 300,000 accounts
have quit.

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:56.901
It's always comforting
when the person who knows all

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:58.801
of your financial information
ghosts you.

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:01.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.567
Well, this is going viral --
at Chipotle,

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:04.501
a customer received an email
from the chain,

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:07.033
saying that they'd won free food
for a year,

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:08.834
but then hours later,
they got another message,

00:05:08.834 --> 00:05:10.167
taking back the offer.

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:11.868
[ Ohhs ]

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:13.067
That's Chipotle for you, huh?

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:14.901
You start super excited,
then a few hours later,

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:16.100
it comes back to haunt you.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.133
[ Laughter and applause ]
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:19.267
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:25.801
On the bright side, when you
hear Chipotle goes viral,

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:27.200
this is the best-case scenario.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:30.701
You guys see this?
Airline crew members

00:05:30.701 --> 00:05:34.334
were caught smuggling 60 pounds
of onions into the Philippines.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.968
[ Laughter ]
The authorities said,

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:38.000
"Are you guys hiding onions?"
And the airline crew was like,

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.000
"[ Sniffles ]
No."

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:43.868 --> 00:05:47.100
Hey, I saw that one company
is looking to hire new workers

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.968
for a pretty interesting job.
Take a look at this.

00:05:48.968 --> 00:05:50.801
-Planters --
they want three people

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:52.901
to be the chauffeur
for Mr. Peanut.

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:55.200
The job starts in June
and requires you

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.501
to drive cross-country
in the Nutmobile.

00:05:57.501 --> 00:06:00.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:02.234 --> 00:06:04.367
[ Drum sting ]

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:05.734
Yeah, they're looking
for new drivers

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:07.400
after the original ones
got sacked.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.734
And --
-Eh oh!

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:13.133
The Nutmobile is just like
the Wienermobile,

00:06:13.133 --> 00:06:15.200
except there's two of them.
-Wey!

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.834
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.434
Fun fact about the Nutmobile --

00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:20.834
as the mileage adds up,
it turns into a lowrider.

00:06:20.834 --> 00:06:22.234
[ Laughter and oohs ]
[ Indistinct ]

00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:23.901
[ Rimshot ]

00:06:23.901 --> 00:06:26.834
Finally, guys, I know a lot
of people find math boring.

00:06:26.834 --> 00:06:29.367
Well, that's why we've updated
math to make the equations

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:30.901
about stuff
that you can relate to.

00:06:30.901 --> 00:06:32.634
It's time for
"Popular Mathematics".

00:06:32.634 --> 00:06:33.801
Here we go.

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:35.734
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:38.634
-♪ Popular Mathematics ♪

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:40.367
♪ Mathematics ♪

00:06:40.367 --> 00:06:41.667
-Yes!

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:42.701
Let's take a look at our first

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:44.100
equation here. If you take...

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:49.868
You see what I'm saying?
-Ah.

00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:51.534
-Meghan Trainor.
-Meghan Trainor, yeah.

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:52.701
-You get the idea.
-Trainor.

00:06:52.701 --> 00:06:53.701
-Here's another one.

00:06:58.133 --> 00:07:01.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:02.434
If you take...

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:09.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:09.133 --> 00:07:10.701
-I see.

00:07:10.701 --> 00:07:12.567
[ Baritone ] Oh, yeah!
-Here's another one.

00:07:18.701 --> 00:07:23.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:25.601
If you take Caesar...
-Yep.

00:07:29.868 --> 00:07:31.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:31.934 --> 00:07:33.701
[ Slurred ]
Hail SZA.

00:07:33.701 --> 00:07:34.701
Here's another one.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.634
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.934
-Popular.

00:07:46.934 --> 00:07:49.133
-If you take Daniel Day-Lewis...
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:52.501 --> 00:07:53.934
♪ Day-o ♪

00:07:53.934 --> 00:07:55.801
[ Laughter ]
♪ Dayyyy-o ♪

00:07:55.801 --> 00:07:58.200
[ Applause ]

00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.501
Here's another one,
A Tesla...

00:08:02.801 --> 00:08:03.734
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:07.601
[ Laughter, oohs, and applause ]

00:08:07.601 --> 00:08:09.167
[ Indistinct ]

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:10.367
And, finally, if you take...

00:08:13.601 --> 00:08:14.868
There you go.
That's all the time we have
-Oh!

00:08:14.868 --> 00:08:16.634
[ Laughter and applause ]
for "Popular Mathematics".

